L300: Objects comparisons are done on textured meshes. SAM 3D is significantly preferred over others on all fronts.
L301: ##### Dataset.
L302: To comprehensively evaluate the model capability under real-world scenarios, we carefully build a new benchmark SA-3DAO, consisting of 1K 3D artist-created meshes created from natural images. We also include ISO3D from 3D Arena (cite163†Ebert, 2025 ) for quantitatively evaluating shape and texture, and Aria Digital Twin (ADT) (cite167†Pan et al., 2023 ) for layout. We further conduct human preference evaluation on two curated sets for both scene-level and object-level reconstruction.
L303: The Pref Set uses real-world images from MetaCLIP (cite168†Xu et al., 2024 ) and SA-1B (cite148†Kirillov et al., 2023 ), as well as a set based on LVIS (cite169†Gupta et al., 2019 ). Refer to cite91†Appendix D for details on evaluation sets.
L304: ##### Settings.
L305: 
L306: We conduct experiments with a Geometry model that is trained to condition on pointmaps. For datasets where pointmaps are unavailable, we estimate them with cite133†Wang et al. (2025a) . We found that shape and texture quality do not depend on whether the model is trained with pointmap conditioning (see cite107†Section E.5 ), but layout (translation/scale) evaluation in cite170†Table 3 requires ground-truth depth/pointmap as reference.
